=== what this comparison does / does not localize ===
  DOES: quantify, from the closed raws only, the observable differences
  at the stage-1 output interface between the unloaded V5 single stage
  and the stage-2-loaded stage-1 (ranges, crossing times/directions,
  same-direction period, crossing slope), and record the stage-2
  clock-device terminal voltages and clock-device currents as saved.
  DOES NOT: localize any difference to a specific device, node, or
  mechanism; does not infer capacitance or a cause from topology alone;
  does not attribute stage-2 reversals to interface loading (a controlled
  load experiment would be required, which is outside this read-only audit).

